  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Viet Nam emergency response to Typhoon Bualoi and Matmo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Viet Nam has triggered emergency response to flooding caused by Typhoon Bualoi and Matmo. Torrential rain has led to severe flooding and landslides. The last two in the six most affected provinces caused 85 deaths, 200 injuries, 546,000 houses damaged/flooded and widespread land inundation; over 180,000 people are estimated to remain in need. The cumulative impacts overwhelmed the government&#x2019;s capacity, hence it has requested international assistance. FCDO contribution to UNICEF will support life-saving assistance in the form of cash assistance, WASH and child protection. UNICEF has arrangements in place to allow a rapid response. As a trusted partner of the government, it will be delivered through national delivery systems, so reinforcing locally led delivery.</narrative>
  </description>
